 ty Fire Authority and AAP-Orange County pediatricians\, to learn how to ke
 ep young children safe in and around water. This free workshop is part of 
 the City's Floatie Exchange Program and will explain why a U.S. Coast Guar
 d-approved life jacket is a safer choice than inflatable floaties. Familie
 s will learn simple\, lifesaving strategies to help prevent drowning and p
 rotect children at pools\, beaches\, lakes\, and other bodies of water. Ch
 ildren who attend with a parent or caregiver will also have the opportunit
 y to be fitted with a properly sized life jacket by the City of Irvine Aqu
 atics Division.\\n\\nMore info: https://irvinepubliclibrary.libcal.com/eve
 nt/17274325
LOCATION:University Park Library Community Room \, University Park Library
URL:https://irvinepubliclibrary.libcal.com/event/17274325
