BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Hunger Action Month Kickoff
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260903T120000
DTSTAMP:20260804T104158Z
UID:0313f2d2d9e852e1d906fc626f1f1289@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Play & Games\\n\\nJoin us for a hands-on community se
 rvice experience with Second Harvest Food Bank of Orange County. Children
  and families will work together to sort and pack fresh produce that will 
 help support neighbors facing food insecurity throughout our community. \
 nTime: 9am-12pm\nIncluded in museum admission. Space is limited! Book yo
 ur tickets now.\n\n*Members do not require a reservation.\n*Events and dat
 es are subject to change. \nAbout the play partner:\nSecond Harvest Food
  Bank is a nonprofit organization in Orange County.\nTheir Vision: Orange 
 County with food and nutritional security for all.\nTheir Mission: In coll
 aboration with our partners\, we provide dignified\, equitable and consist
 ent access to nutritious food\, creating a foundation for community health
 .\nTheir Value: Integrity\, accountability\, people first\, compassion\, p
 urpose driven\, stewardship \nFrequently Asked Questions\n\nWho can part
 icipate?\nChildren and families of all ages are welcome to help pack produ
 ce alongside the Second Harvest Food Bank team.\n\nDo I need any special e
 xperience?\nNo experience is needed. Second Harvest staff and volunteers
  will provide instructions and guidance throughout the activity.\n\nWhat w
 ill we be doing?\nFamilies will help sort and pack fresh produce that will
  be distributed to local children\, families\, and seniors experiencing fo
 od insecurity\n\nWhy is Pretend City hosting this event?\nAs part of Hung
 er Action Month\, we&#8217\;re helping children learn that they can make a
  positive impact in their community through acts of kindness and service\n
 \nHow does this support child development?\nChildren practice counting\, s
 orting\, teamwork\, problem-solving\, and fine motor skills while learning
  empathy\, generosity\, and community responsibility\n\nIs there an addit
 ional cost to participate?\nNo. This activity is included with museum adm
 ission\n\nCan my child participate for only part of the event?\nYes. Fa
 milies are welcome to stop by anytime between 9:00 AM and 12:00 PM\n\nWhe
 re does the food go?\nThe packed produce will be distributed through Secon
 d Harvest Food Bank&#8217\;s network of community partners serving familie
 s throughout Orange County\n\nHow many families can participate?\nPartici
 pation is available on a first-come\, first-served basis while supplies la
 st.\\n\\nMore info: https://www.pretendcity.org/events/hunger-action-month
 -kickoff/
LOCATION:Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\, 29 Hubble\, Irvine\, CA
 \, 92618
URL:https://www.pretendcity.org/events/hunger-action-month-kickoff/
BEGIN:VALARM
ACTION:DISPLAY
DESCRIPTION:Tomorrow: Hunger Action Month Kickoff
TRIGGER:-P1D
END:VALARM
